@page "/"

<PageTitle>Production Intelligence</PageTitle>

<div class="page">
    <div class="page-head">
        <h1>Production Intelligence System</h1>
        <span class="muted">Turns line events into actions, shared fixes and better skills.</span>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:0;max-width:75ch;line-height:1.55;">
        A clickable prototype of the three role views from the concept brief. All numbers are sample data for a six-line
        tissue converting hall. In the real system they come from the PLC project (counts, speed, stops), the Voice project
        (stop reasons, transcripts, “what fixed it?”), the planner’s daily target and the shift roster.
    </p>
    <div class="roles">
        <a class="card role-card" href="operator">
            <h2>Operator</h2>
            <p>One number: the pace needed to hit the shift target. When the line stops, the top approved fixes. After restart, one tap: did it work?</p>
            <span class="small" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">Open line-side screen</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card role-card" href="shift-leader">
            <h2>Shift leader</h2>
            <p>Live board of every line, patrol priorities, manpower flags, fix approvals and a drafted handover ready to check and send.</p>
            <span class="small" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">Open live board</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card role-card" href="section-head">
            <h2>Section head</h2>
            <p>Weekly AI digest, repeat losses with countermeasures judged from PLC data, shift and line comparisons, and plain-language questions.</p>
            <span class="small" style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;">Open weekly view</span>
        </a>
    </div>
    <section class="card">
        <h2>Guardrails shown in the prototype</h2>
        <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;">
            <li>Operators only see fixes a shift leader approved, each with its source.</li>
            <li>A suggestion that bypasses a guard or lockout is blocked and cannot be approved.</li>
            <li>Points reward complete logs, problems fixed for good and shared fixes, not raw output.</li>
            <li>Skills and shift comparisons are framed for training, not ranking.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
